> meatballs, and is growing increasingly less tame as we go.  What sort
> of things does a winged snake like to eat?

No "A" creature eats anything.  You can't reward it to get
it to steal items for you.  This is an issue with all types
of pets that don't eat.

Unless you are doing things from a certain list, your pet
isn't getting less tame.  Pets have two different numbers
that describe their behavior: tameness and aport.  The
tameness only goes down with certain acts (which does
include exploring other levels long enough so keep your
pets with you).  The aport goes down every time your pet
drops an item.

Monsters that don't eat will eventually stop picking up
items they don't want for themselves and there is not way
to change that except more polymorph.  But there is a huge
up-side to this issue.  Many non-eating monsters are much
more powerfull than any type of dog, cat or horse.  All
of the "A" monsters are powerfull.



